# What EAS Build must NOT upload.
#
# EAS archives from the repository root, because a package.json lives here — so
# without this it tars the entire monorepo. Two problems with that: the upload
# carries four applications the mobile build has no use for, and
# backend/public/storage is a symlink that Windows cannot recreate inside the
# build's temp clone, which fails the upload outright:
#
#   EPERM: operation not permitted, symlink
#   'D:\Caretime\backend\storage\app\public' -> '...\backend\public\storage'
#
# Only mobile-app/ is needed to build the app.

backend/
frontend/
desktop/
marketing/
browser-extension/
docs/
scripts/
.github/
.playwright-mcp/

# Build output and archives that are large and never needed.
**/node_modules/
**/vendor/
**/.git/
*.pdf
*.png
*.apk
*.aab
